00:00:00,103 --> 00:00:05,039
Turning Evidence into a Thesis My thesis examined the adoption of a

2
00:00:05,053 --> 00:00:10,632
new teaching method I had to formulate a proposition explain its derivation

3
00:00:10,882 --> 00:00:15,500
and identify what would count as supporting evidence The first draft was

4
00:00:15,513 --> 00:00:18,882
deficient in detail and relied on an analogy that did not fit

5
00:00:18,895 --> 00:00:23,513
the data My supervisor asked me to distinguish a constituent of the

6
00:00:23,526 --> 00:00:27,605
model from an assumption about the whole I should not postulate a

7
00:00:27,618 --> 00:00:32,658
mechanism merely to explain away an inconvenient result Nor could I claim

8
00:00:32,671 --> 00:00:36,908
that two trends must correlate simply because their timing happened to coincide

9
00:00:37,816 --> 00:00:42,579
I revised the formulation placed extra tables in an appendix and prepared

10
00:00:42,592 --> 00:00:47,803
a synthesis of the findings The conclusion acknowledged a marginal effect and

11
00:00:47,816 --> 00:00:53,263
a substantial limitation The process was demanding but it helped me appreciate

12
00:00:53,276 --> 00:00:58,632
why rigorous expression matters A sound argument remains open to revision when

13
00:00:58,645 --> 00:01:00,816
new evidence challenges its premises
